:techniqueDFT-1200
    a owl:Class,
      solveit-core:Technique ;
    rdfs:label "DFT-1200: Evaluate observations in light of hypotheses"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf solveit-core:SolveitInvestigativeAction ;
    solveit-core:techniqueID "DFT-1200" ;
    solveit-core:techniqueName "Evaluate observations in light of hypotheses" ;
    solveit-core:techniqueDescription "The process of assessing the probability or strength of the observations under each of two or more competing hypotheses, and expressing the strength of support for one over another." ;
    solveit-core:techniqueDetails "In evaluative mode the hypotheses are fixed before evaluation begins and are taken as given, typically from DFT-1195; this technique does not formulate or revise them. The examiner assesses how probable or strong the observations are under each hypothesis in turn, assuming each to be true. Assigning a probability or strength to the observations under a hypothesis requires knowledge of how the system behaves under that hypothesis, drawn from DFT-1090 or from published data. The technique concludes with the strength of support expressed as a likelihood ratio, its verbal equivalent, or other method. Conveying that opinion is DFT-1093." ;
    solveit-core:hasSynonym "Evaluative interpretation",
                            "Evidence evaluation",
                            "Likelihood ratio assessment",
                            "Scientific interpretation" ;
    solveit-core:hasCASEInputClass solveit-analysis:HypothesisSet,
                                   uco-observable:Observable ;
    solveit-core:hasCASEOutputClass <https://ontology.unifiedcyberontology.org/uco/analysis/AnalyticResult> ;
    solveit-core:hasPotentialWeakness :weaknessDFW-1403,
                                      :weaknessDFW-1404,
                                      :weaknessDFW-1405,
                                      :weaknessDFW-1406,
                                      :weaknessDFW-1407 ;
    solveit-core:hasReference :citationDFCite-1163,
                              :citationDFCite-1164,
                              :citationDFCite-1165 .

