:techniqueDFT-1204
    a owl:Class,
      solveit-core:Technique ;
    rdfs:label "DFT-1204: Verify hash of stored bitstream data matches a stored hash"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf solveit-core:SolveitInvestigativeAction ;
    solveit-core:techniqueID "DFT-1204" ;
    solveit-core:techniqueName "Verify hash of stored bitstream data matches a stored hash" ;
    solveit-core:techniqueDescription "Compares a hash computed over stored bitstream data against a recorded hash, to assess whether the stored data has changed since it was written." ;
    solveit-core:techniqueDetails """The stored hash may be held inside the forensic image container, in an associated text file, or in a separate trusted location. 

The same comparison applies in each case. The hash over the stored data is produced by DFT-1199 (Compute hash of stored bitstream data), and a hash held inside a container is read using DFT-1193 (Read metadata from within a forensic image container). 

This technique covers verification carried out after imaging has finished, whereas DFT-1042 (Verify hash of copied data matches the hash of the data read from source device) covers the comparison made *during imaging* against a hash of data read from the source device.""" ;
    solveit-core:hasExample "ewfverify" ;
    solveit-core:hasCASEInputClass <https://ontology.unifiedcyberontology.org/uco/types/Hash> ;
    solveit-core:hasCASEOutputClass solveit-observable:HashVerificationResult ;
    solveit-core:hasPotentialWeakness :weaknessDFW-1042,
                                      :weaknessDFW-1127,
                                      :weaknessDFW-1128 ;
    solveit-core:hasReference :citationDFCite-1168 .

:techniqueDFT-1205
    a owl:Class,
      solveit-core:Technique ;
    rdfs:label "DFT-1205: Decode raw data into data value(s)"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf solveit-core:SolveitInvestigativeAction ;
    solveit-core:techniqueID "DFT-1205" ;
    solveit-core:techniqueName "Decode raw data into data value(s)" ;
    solveit-core:techniqueDescription "The process of interpreting a sequence of bytes as a typed value, such as a number, a string, or a date, under an assumed encoding." ;
    solveit-core:techniqueDetails """Decoding is performed inside many other techniques rather than as a separate examination step, which is why its failures are currently recorded against whichever technique consumed the value. This provides a generic version of the technique. 

Related techniques that depend on it include DFT-1191 (Parse allocated structures in Windows HIVE files), DFT-1071 (Extract data from SQLite database(s)) and DFT-1121 (Index a data source for keyword searching). DFT-1044 and DFT-1102 decode specific container formats rather than typed values. """ ;
    solveit-core:hasCASEInputClass uco-observable:ContentData ;
    solveit-core:hasPotentialWeakness :weaknessDFW-1456 ;
    solveit-core:hasSubtechnique :techniqueDFT-1206,
                                 :techniqueDFT-1207 .

:techniqueDFT-1206
    a owl:Class,
      solveit-core:Technique ;
    rdfs:label "DFT-1206: Decode a number from raw data"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf :techniqueDFT-1205 ;
    solveit-core:techniqueID "DFT-1206" ;
    solveit-core:techniqueName "Decode a number from raw data" ;
    solveit-core:techniqueDescription "The process of interpreting a sequence of bytes as a numeric value under an assumed width, signedness, and byte order." ;
    solveit-core:techniqueDetails """Numeric decoding underlies most structured parsing, for example DFT-1191 (Parse allocated structures in Windows HIVE files), where values such as REG_DWORD and REG_QWORD are stored as raw integers. 

This technique groups numbers together to include signed and unsigned, integers and floats, different endianness, and number of bytes considered in the decoding.

Note that strings and timestamps are considered in separate techniques. 
""" ;
    solveit-core:hasCASEInputClass uco-observable:ContentData ;
    solveit-core:hasPotentialWeakness :weaknessDFW-1457,
                                      :weaknessDFW-1458,
                                      :weaknessDFW-1459,
                                      :weaknessDFW-1460,
                                      :weaknessDFW-1461,
                                      :weaknessDFW-1462,
                                      :weaknessDFW-1463,
                                      :weaknessDFW-1464,
                                      :weaknessDFW-1465 .

:techniqueDFT-1207
    a owl:Class,
      solveit-core:Technique ;
    rdfs:label "DFT-1207: Decode a string from raw data"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf :techniqueDFT-1205 ;
    solveit-core:techniqueID "DFT-1207" ;
    solveit-core:techniqueName "Decode a string from raw data" ;
    solveit-core:techniqueDescription "The process of decoding a sequence of bytes as text under an assumed character encoding." ;
    solveit-core:techniqueDetails """

""" ;
    solveit-core:hasSynonym "text decoding" ;
    solveit-core:hasCASEInputClass uco-observable:ContentData ;
    solveit-core:hasPotentialWeakness :weaknessDFW-1466,
                                      :weaknessDFW-1467,
                                      :weaknessDFW-1468,
                                      :weaknessDFW-1469,
                                      :weaknessDFW-1470,
                                      :weaknessDFW-1471,
                                      :weaknessDFW-1472 .

:techniqueDFT-1208
    a owl:Class,
      solveit-core:Technique ;
    rdfs:label "DFT-1208: Store acquisition metadata along with a forensic image format"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf solveit-core:SolveitInvestigativeAction ;
    solveit-core:techniqueID "DFT-1208" ;
    solveit-core:techniqueName "Store acquisition metadata along with a forensic image format" ;
    solveit-core:techniqueDescription "Records details such as case and examiner details, and the acquisition hash, with a forensic image container alongside the bitstream data or logical files. " ;
    solveit-core:techniqueDetails """This is the counterpart of DFT-1193, which reads these same values back. 

Container formats such as EWF and AFF4 carry a case number, evidence number, examiner name, notes and description, together with the cryptographic hash computed during acquisition. 

DFT-1025 stores the bitstream itself, whereas this technique records the metadata that accompanies it. The hash written here is the value later verified against by DFT-1204. 

Metadata accompanying a raw image is held in a separate file rather than within a container, and is not covered by this technique.""" ;
    solveit-core:hasExample "ewfacquire" ;
    solveit-core:hasCASEInputClass <https://ontology.unifiedcyberontology.org/uco/types/Hash>,
                                   case-investigation:exhibitNumber,
                                   solveit-observable:LogicalImageContainer,
                                   solveit-observable:PhysicalImageContainer,
                                   uco-core:description,
                                   uco-core:name,
                                   uco-observable:Note ;
    solveit-core:hasCASEOutputClass solveit-observable:LogicalImageContainer,
                                    solveit-observable:PhysicalImageContainer ;
    solveit-core:hasPotentialWeakness :weaknessDFW-1473,
                                      :weaknessDFW-1474,
                                      :weaknessDFW-1475,
                                      :weaknessDFW-1476,
                                      :weaknessDFW-1477,
                                      :weaknessDFW-1478 .

:techniqueDFT-1209
    a owl:Class,
      solveit-core:Technique ;
    rdfs:label "DFT-1209: Extract artifacts from data provided by a service provider"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf solveit-core:SolveitInvestigativeAction ;
    solveit-core:techniqueID "DFT-1209" ;
    solveit-core:techniqueName "Extract artifacts from data provided by a service provider" ;
    solveit-core:techniqueDescription "Parse data supplied by an online service provider into artifacts such as messages, accounts, contacts and events." ;
    solveit-core:techniqueDetails "Covers data supplied to law enforcement in response to legal process (see DFT-1024) and data supplied by the provider to the account holder, e.g. Google Takeout or Meta 'Download Your Information'. Formats and field meanings differ between providers and change over time." ;
    solveit-core:hasSynonym "Legal process return",
                            "Production order response",
                            "Search warrant return",
                            "Warrant return processing" ;
    solveit-core:hasCASEInputClass solveit-observable:FileSet,
                                   uco-observable:ArchiveFile ;
    solveit-core:hasCASEOutputClass solveit-observable:ArtifactSet .

:techniqueDFT-1210
    a owl:Class,
      solveit-core:Technique ;
    rdfs:label "DFT-1210: Obtain approval for a digital forensic activity"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf solveit-core:SolveitInvestigativeAction ;
    solveit-core:techniqueID "DFT-1210" ;
    solveit-core:techniqueName "Obtain approval for a digital forensic activity" ;
    solveit-core:techniqueDescription "Obtain the legal or organisational authorisation required before a digital forensic activity can be carried out, e.g. a search warrant, production order or internal sign-off." ;
    solveit-core:hasSynonym "Obtain a production order",
                            "Obtain a search warrant",
                            "Obtain authorisation" ;
    solveit-core:hasExample "Search warrant application approved by a magistrate (US)" ;
    solveit-core:hasCASEOutputClass case-investigation:Authorization .

:techniqueDFT-1211
    a owl:Class,
      solveit-core:Technique ;
    rdfs:label "DFT-1211: Create a case-type keyword list"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf solveit-core:SolveitInvestigativeAction ;
    solveit-core:techniqueID "DFT-1211" ;
    solveit-core:techniqueName "Create a case-type keyword list" ;
    solveit-core:techniqueDescription "The process of compiling a reusable list of keywords associated with a particular type of offense or investigation, for use in later keyword searches." ;
    solveit-core:techniqueDetails "Case-type keyword lists are typically prepared in advance of any specific investigation and maintained over time, for example a list of terms associated with drug supply, fraud, or child sexual exploitation. They capture the vocabulary, slang, code words, and abbreviations typically used in that type of case. The output is consumed by keyword searching using case-type wordlists (DFT-1122). This differs from creating a case-specific keyword list, which is built from the details of an individual case, and from creating a password dictionary, which serves a different purpose and has different quality criteria." ;
    solveit-core:hasSynonym "case-type wordlist",
                            "offense-type keyword list" ;
    solveit-core:hasCASEOutputClass solveit-observable:Wordlist ;
    solveit-core:hasPotentialWeakness :weaknessDFW-1479,
                                      :weaknessDFW-1480,
                                      :weaknessDFW-1481 ;
    solveit-core:hasReference :citationDFCite-1074 .

:techniqueDFT-1212
    a owl:Class,
      solveit-core:Technique ;
    rdfs:label "DFT-1212: Create a case-specific keyword list"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf solveit-core:SolveitInvestigativeAction ;
    solveit-core:techniqueID "DFT-1212" ;
    solveit-core:techniqueName "Create a case-specific keyword list" ;
    solveit-core:techniqueDescription "The process of compiling a list of keywords derived from the details of a specific case, such as names, places, usernames, and other identifiers, for use in keyword searches." ;
    solveit-core:techniqueDetails "Case-specific keyword lists are usually derived from the case brief, witness statements, and other case material, and may be extended as new identifiers emerge during the examination. Typical entries include names of people and organizations, nicknames, addresses, telephone numbers, email addresses, account names, and transaction references. The output is consumed by keyword searching using case-specific wordlists (DFT-1123). This complements case-type keyword lists. Case-specific information may also be used as input when creating a password dictionary." ;
    solveit-core:hasSynonym "case-specific wordlist" ;
    solveit-core:hasCASEOutputClass solveit-observable:Wordlist ;
    solveit-core:hasPotentialWeakness :weaknessDFW-1482,
                                      :weaknessDFW-1483,
                                      :weaknessDFW-1484 ;
    solveit-core:hasReference :citationDFCite-1074 .

:techniqueDFT-1213
    a owl:Class,
      solveit-core:Technique ;
    rdfs:label "DFT-1213: Generate reference data by performing and recording actions"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf solveit-core:SolveitInvestigativeAction ;
    solveit-core:techniqueID "DFT-1213" ;
    solveit-core:techniqueName "Generate reference data by performing and recording actions" ;
    solveit-core:techniqueDescription "The process of deliberately performing known actions on a system and recording exactly what was done, how and when, so that the record is ground truth for the traces those actions leave." ;
    solveit-core:techniqueDetails "Each recorded action is one piece of ground truth, for example \"file A copied to B by byte copy, between 10:02:03.120 and 10:02:03.141 on the recording host's clock\". Record the exact method used (system call, command or user-interface gesture), since different methods leave different traces, and the environment (operating system, version, drivers, hardware) and clock. The technique is commonly the first part of DFT-1090, followed by preserving the resulting data (DFT-1110, e.g. imaging the system) and analysing the traces; it is also used to build test data for tool testing and datasets, where the behaviour is already known. Its output is the record of the actions, not a conclusion about what traces they leave: working out which traces came from which action is part of DFT-1090." ;
    solveit-core:hasSynonym "Create ground truth data",
                            "Generate activity-based reference data" ;
    solveit-core:hasExample "Automatically exercising an app after each update to generate reference data [DFCite-1034]",
                            "Building a labelled dataset by performing scripted user-interface actions on an app in a virtual machine, each action recorded as it is performed",
                            "Building a test image for tool testing by performing a planned sequence of file system operations on a test volume, recording each with its method, start and end times" ;
    solveit-core:hasCASEInputClass uco-action:ActionPattern ;
    solveit-core:hasCASEOutputClass uco-action:ActionLifecycle ;
    solveit-core:hasPotentialWeakness :weaknessDFW-1148 ;
    solveit-core:hasReference :citationDFCite-1034 .

:techniqueDFT-1215
    a owl:Class,
      solveit-core:Technique ;
    rdfs:label "DFT-1215: Store content in logical forensic container file(s)"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf solveit-core:SolveitInvestigativeAction ;
    solveit-core:techniqueID "DFT-1215" ;
    solveit-core:techniqueName "Store content in logical forensic container file(s)" ;
    solveit-core:techniqueDescription "Storage of a set of files and their metadata within a logical forensic container format such as L01, AD1, CTR or AFF4-L." ;
    solveit-core:techniqueDetails """Logical container formats store a selected set of files together with file system metadata such as paths, timestamps, sizes and other attributes. Depending on the format, they may also store hashes of individual files and case information. 

This technique represents storage of files in a logical container, whereas DFT-1025 represents storage of bitstream data in a physical image format. The contents of the container are read back using DFT-1170.

This differs from a simple archive format e.g. DFT-1026 in that forensic specific additions are made e.g. storage of metadata, hashes or provenance, but it does not preclude an archive format being used for the container. 

Formats differ in which metadata they are able to record, so some metadata present on the source may not be retained in the container.""" ;
    solveit-core:hasSynonym "Create logical evidence file",
                            "Create logical image",
                            "Store files in a logical container",
                            "Write files to a logical image format" ;
    solveit-core:hasExample "AFF4-L: logical extension to AFF4 for storing files and their metadata (Cohen, Garfinkel and Schatz, 2009)",
                            "EnCase: can create logical evidence files (L01/Lx01) from selected files",
                            "FTK Imager: can create AD1 custom content images from selected files and folders",
                            "X-Ways Forensics: can create evidence file containers (.ctr)" ;
    solveit-core:hasCASEInputClass solveit-observable:FileSet ;
    solveit-core:hasCASEOutputClass solveit-observable:LogicalImageContainer ;
    solveit-core:hasReference :citationDFCite-1035,
                              :citationDFCite-1069 .

