:weaknessDFW-1380
    a solveit-core:Weakness ;
    rdfs:label "DFW-1380: A proposed hypothesis suffers from a lack of falsifiability"@en ;
    solveit-core:weaknessID "DFW-1380" ;
    solveit-core:weaknessName "A proposed hypothesis suffers from a lack of falsifiability" ;
    solveit-core:weaknessDescription "A scientifically valid hypothesis must present an outcome that can be definitively proven false." ;
    solveit-core:hasWeaknessClass solveit-core:ASTM_MISINT ;
    solveit-core:hasPotentialMitigation :mitigationDFM-1301 .

:weaknessDFW-1381
    a solveit-core:Weakness ;
    rdfs:label "DFW-1381: A proposed hypothesis equates correlation with causation"@en ;
    solveit-core:weaknessID "DFW-1381" ;
    solveit-core:weaknessName "A proposed hypothesis equates correlation with causation" ;
    solveit-core:weaknessDescription "Causal mechanisms are not explicitly established" ;
    solveit-core:hasWeaknessClass solveit-core:ASTM_MISINT ;
    solveit-core:hasPotentialMitigation :mitigationDFM-1302 .

:weaknessDFW-1382
    a solveit-core:Weakness ;
    rdfs:label "DFW-1382: A hypothesis refers to \"device user\" rather than \"suspect\" when a specific individual is under investigation"@en ;
    solveit-core:weaknessID "DFW-1382" ;
    solveit-core:weaknessName "A hypothesis refers to \"device user\" rather than \"suspect\" when a specific individual is under investigation" ;
    solveit-core:weaknessDescription "When a specific individual is under investigation, address this fact. If the individual's use of a device is challenged, this should be explicitly addressed in hypothesis generation." ;
    solveit-core:hasWeaknessClass solveit-core:ASTM_MISINT ;
    solveit-core:hasPotentialMitigation :mitigationDFM-1303 .

:weaknessDFW-1383
    a solveit-core:Weakness ;
    rdfs:label "DFW-1383: A proposed hypothesis uses judgmental or loaded terminology"@en ;
    solveit-core:weaknessID "DFW-1383" ;
    solveit-core:weaknessName "A proposed hypothesis uses judgmental or loaded terminology" ;
    solveit-core:weaknessDescription "Judgmental or loaded terminology is outside the scope of digital forensics and could reflect bias" ;
    solveit-core:hasWeaknessClass solveit-core:ASTM_MISINT ;
    solveit-core:hasPotentialMitigation :mitigationDFM-1304 .

:weaknessDFW-1384
    a solveit-core:Weakness ;
    rdfs:label "DFW-1384: Addressing the wrong level of the hierarchy of hypotheses required for the case"@en ;
    solveit-core:weaknessID "DFW-1384" ;
    solveit-core:weaknessName "Addressing the wrong level of the hierarchy of hypotheses required for the case" ;
    solveit-core:weaknessDescription "The hierarchy of hypotheses (a.k.a. hierarchy of propositions) are: 1) source level concerns where a trace came from (e.g., which device produced contraband), 2) activity level concerns what act produced it (e.g., who produced contraband), and 3) offense level concerns the criminal issue itself (e.g., whether the suspect knowingly produced contraband) — with higher levels being more relevant to decision-makers but requiring more case information to evaluate." ;
    solveit-core:hasWeaknessClass solveit-core:ASTM_MISINT ;
    solveit-core:hasPotentialMitigation :mitigationDFM-1305 .

:weaknessDFW-1385
    a solveit-core:Weakness ;
    rdfs:label "DFW-1385: A proposed hypothesis uses vague or complex phrasing"@en ;
    solveit-core:weaknessID "DFW-1385" ;
    solveit-core:weaknessName "A proposed hypothesis uses vague or complex phrasing" ;
    solveit-core:weaknessDescription "Hypotheses are declarative statements written in the present tense, without ambiguous language, multiple conditions, or conditional verbs (e.g., \"if-then\" or \"would\"). " ;
    solveit-core:hasWeaknessClass solveit-core:ASTM_MISINT ;
    solveit-core:hasPotentialMitigation :mitigationDFM-1306 .

:weaknessDFW-1386
    a solveit-core:Weakness ;
    rdfs:label "DFW-1386: A proposed hypothesis is overly specific to details in the case"@en ;
    solveit-core:weaknessID "DFW-1386" ;
    solveit-core:weaknessName "A proposed hypothesis is overly specific to details in the case" ;
    solveit-core:weaknessDescription "Generating hypotheses that focus on specific details available early in an investigation can be too narrow to accomodate new details found later, and increases the risk of confirmation bias, such as focusing on the use of a specific wiping tool rather than any wiping tool being used" ;
    solveit-core:hasWeaknessClass solveit-core:ASTM_MISINT ;
    solveit-core:hasPotentialMitigation :mitigationDFM-1307 .

